A||N||5||jhogans||How can I get a Firebird face put on my Fiero?||||5||
Z||000000||jhogans||05-10-2000||09:20 PM||||How can I get a Firebird face put on my Fiero?  I've been thinking about getting another fiero and doing a kit conversion.  I wouldn't mind doing a kit that looks like a mid-engine version of the Firebird.  Something that a future Fiero may look like.<P><BR>Check out these picture.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.1le.net/images/bobs.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.1le.net/images/bobs.jpg</A>  <BR>   <A HREF="http://www.socal-fbodies.org/members/fntarnold.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.socal-fbodies.org/members/fntarnold.html</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://www.socal-fbodies.org/members/cmartin.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.socal-fbodies.org/members/cmartin.html</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://www.socal-fbodies.org/members/hguindi.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.socal-fbodies.org/members/hguindi.html</A> <P><BR>Check out those nostrils.<P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by jhogans (edited 05-10-2000).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||Haze_Performance||05-10-2000||09:27 PM||||With a good body shop and DEEP pockets you can do anything. <P><BR>Right now im working on bonding a 97 style WS6 Ram Air scoop on my hood....||||reg||1
